The UUCP queue for the smart-host named in /dd/SYS/UUCP/Parameters.`uucphost', `inhost' and `newshost' in that file all say `seabass', and theUUCP tools queue work for a site in <spooldir>/<sitename> -- so thisdirectory has to exist before any of them can put anything in it.  Withoutit, `rmail nowhere!somebody' stops with    rmail: doremote: can't change to spool directory: seabass...error #216and `postnews' stops the same way.  With it, `rmail' queues a real job:a C. command file, a D. data file, and a D. file for the local system.Nothing here sends anything.  os9exec presents no serial line, so the worksits in this directory until a `uucico' that has one comes for it.  Deletewhat accumulates whenever you like; these are ordinary files.